# X02 kernel evidence: FP8 kernels run in the Qwen + LoRA training step

FP8 run `smoke-fp8_te`, control `smoke-bf16_te`. Both profiled for one effective update (4 microbatches x 8 x 512 tokens, forward + backward + optimizer) with torch.profiler (CUDA activity via CUPTI). Kernel classes are name-based (`fp8_backend.classify_kernel`); the FP8-only set below is a direct diff against the control and does not depend on the classifier.

TE 2.20.2, `transformer_engine.pytorch.autocast`, recipe {'amax_compute_algo': 'max', 'amax_history_len': 16, 'fp8_format': 'HYBRID', 'margin': 0, 'name': 'delayed_scaling'}, fp8_available=False. 196 of 197 nn.Linear converted (decoder q/k/v/o/gate/up/down x 28 layers); lm_head (tied embedding) stays eager BF16.

| kernel class | FP8 run calls | FP8 run ms | control calls | control ms |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| FP8 GEMM | 784 | 35.07 | 0 | 0.00 |
| FP8 cast / amax / scaling | 2348 | 32.74 | 0 | 0.00 |
| non-FP8 GEMM | 2344 | 84.52 | 3128 | 174.65 |
| other kernels | 17956 | 267.27 | 18300 | 276.83 |

